hey what's up my name's samuel leeds and  this is a message directly to the bbc  because they are doing yet another  documentary i don't know if it's going  to be about me this time but here's the  thing  they have exposed themself  probably by mistake last week and to be  honest i am  absolutely baffled mind-blown  at sea what i'm about to reveal to you  is shocking because when i  read that post the bbc's post last week  when they're trying to do their  undercover investigations  and they exposed themselves i thought it  was really interesting because they did  a show about me the bbc  i did a whole video about this and this  was in january so about eight months ago  and to be honest when they did the show  i thought this is such bad reporting  i just can't understand how this has  happened have they deliberately  come in with an agenda they must have  done but i found it really strange  because i always grew up thinking  the bbc were fair we're neutral and i  thought they would always  put both sides across and i just thought  they never spoke to me beforehand  they out of all of my thousands and  thousands of students  they chose two unhappy students and i'm  like this is  crazy why and how has this happened well  folks  now i know and bbc to be honest i know  you've always ignored me in the past i  know you've not responded to my previous  video i asked you a ton of questions but  i really think  that the public as we pay so much money  to you bbc as you force everybody  in the country pretty much to contribute  to your journalism  and to your reporting skills and in the  disguise of putting together a balanced  fair view to inform people  i think you really have a lot of  explaining to do  after last week's post so just to set a  little bit of background  the bbc are doing yet another  documentary  on training companies that teach money  so not many companies teach money you  grow up all through school and you do  not learn about money you go to  university you do not learn about money  but the businesses such as my business  that teach people how to invest and how  to make money  have been absolutely penalized by the  media  over the last six eight months and it's  almost like they're trying to stop  people  wanting to become financially illiterate  and i'll talk about that later  but rather than posting and saying hey  we're looking to do a documentary on  people  on people that have gone through wealth  creation courses  property investment training courses can  you come and get in touch if you've had  an experience  they don't say that what they say is  they say please get in touch if  you've had a bad experience  i mean that is absolutely crazy  imagine if i said i'm doing a  documentary on universities  i'm doing and to see whether  universities are good or not  please could you get in touch with me if  you've been through university and you  were left unhappy would that not  make me look like a complete amateur  that had an agenda and my agenda is  clearly  just to speak to unhappy people i mean  it's absolutely insane  they have completely exposed their  agenda and you might say  yeah samuel whatever samuel you've got  your own agenda or saying  but just re read what they posted this  was on linkedin  three days ago bbc business is looking  into online training courses that claim  to offer a fast track to  financial independence but actually  provide little value for money  okay have you spent hundreds or even  thousands of pounds on these courses  but now feel the training didn't match  up to the promises you were made  if this is something that has impacted  you we would like to hear your story  comment below if you're happy for us to  contact you  so so they're not saying contact us if  you're happy contact us if you've been  through the training  we only want to hear from you if you're  unhappy  and the bbc i started running some  online training courses over lockdown  and we've had thousands and thousands  of students come through the online  training and we have had  a tiny fraction i think we've only had  five people that have said actually  contacted them and said they weren't  happy  out of thousands and what the bbc are  trying to do is they're trying to find  those five  they're trying to find those five  because it's very easy to see you look  on my youtube channel you see  every single week people becoming  financially free it's very easy you go  on  my review site and you see thousands of  reviews  and most of the time these are five out  of five  but what they're doing is they're  specifically targeting the unhappy ones  to paint a narrative how shocking is  that and then people  have commented under the post and said i  had an unhappy experience  or i've i've got some experience with  these training companies and they  weren't good  christopher p who is running this and  producing the show  says i'd love you to add me on linkedin  so we can chat and i can hear your  experience  however interestingly when i tried to  add christopher p  on linkedin it's been three days  christopher p i'm still  waiting for your acceptance why do you  not want to speak to me  why do you not want to speak to any of  my happy customers  or any happy customers that have gone  through this at all let me tell you  something  i don't know exactly what the agenda is  maybe they're just trying to create bad  news stories but there is a reason  that the bbc want to get a particular  message across to you  and want to put you off and you scared  of becoming financially literate  the rich are getting richer the poor are  getting poorer and there's a reason that  we don't teach kids about money in  school  and there's a reason that anybody that  starts teaching about wealth gets  shut down and you know what i'd love to  know what the answer is so bbc  if you're doing a documentary about  online training and wealth creation  i run the biggest wealth creation  company in the uk  so why don't we have a conversation and  i can give you anything you need without  you having to do your little narrative  and and try and fish for those five  unhappy customers oh by the way  if you've been through my training  you've been through my online training  courses  why don't you add christopher p on  linkedin and tell him  your experience if it's good or if it's  bad it doesn't matter just  tell him your experience because i think  it's unfair and i don't think it's right  that the bbc are only looking for  unhappy customers so add christopher p  on linkedin  telling your experience bad or good  and tell them the truth and if you  haven't done any training and you're  like well i don't even know what the  situation is  it just shows you cannot listen to the  media because the media have a  very hard agenda so you need to  make up your own mind anyway i just  wanted to get this out there christopher  p  i hope to hear from you also that last  lady abby jayola they did a whole show  about me  and you did a documentary about me i'm  still waiting for you to respond to my  questions  why don't we do a financial freedom  challenge together and you can spend a  week with me  you can even bring your cameras and then  you can see actually how this works and  if it's possible or not  or you can just carry on making up  stories for a living i don't know  but to be honest i think this needs to  stop i think as the bbc  spend i think i read somewhere they  spend 100 million a year on advertising  so they're spending a hundred million a  year to advertise  they're taking everybody's money from  the country  but they're forcing and i mean some i've  heard some people call them now the  british brainwashing channel and i used  to think that's offensive and that's not  fair  how can you say that about the bbc to be  honest bbc i'm beginning to lose faith  in you right now so get in touch  let's have a conversation thanks for  watching add christopher p  tell him what you think subscribe smash  the like button tell me what you think  in the comments  what do you think make up your mind bbc  look forward to hearing from you

